{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-104478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/assets/8d940d158c631143a1fe7652a4fb83bf2f67f3fd4bbdbbc4a33643bd282b5028.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-104478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(-1+2\\text{i}))(x-(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(-1-2\\text{i})-x(-1+2\\text{i})+(-1+2\\text{i})(-1-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}+2x+5) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-104478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9573aca0153e9509d90542c4195918d4d6d289707f325d2389a641af001e733c"} {"question" "q-104478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-104478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+5x+4"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+8x"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x+16"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-104478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+20x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-107538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,{x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-107538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-5) \\\\  & =2(x+2)(x+2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+2)(x+2)(x-5) & =2({x}^{2}+4x+4)(x-5) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2}+4x-20x-20) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-107538" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9573aca0153e9509d90542c4195918d4d6d289707f325d2389a641af001e733c"} {"question" "q-107538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-107538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+32x-20"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-16x-35"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-32x-40"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-16x-20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-107538" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-32x-40"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-316626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,{x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-316626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=3,$ ${x}_{2}=3,$ and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-3)(x-3)(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =5(x-3)(x-3)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-3)(x-3)(x+2) & =5({x}^{2}-6x+9)(x+2) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}-12x+9x+18) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-3x+18) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-15x+90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-15x+90.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-316626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9573aca0153e9509d90542c4195918d4d6d289707f325d2389a641af001e733c"} {"question" "q-316626" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005293/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef14331e04c6d28adbb583495b3f14da60285ce4273c93b0531610c105608fed"} {"question" "q-316626" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] 